  "foaf:name": "Congolese Estuaries Monitoring",
  "sdo:name": "Congolese Estuaries Monitoring",
  "sdo:description": "The estuaries along the Congolese coast, essential for biodiversity and fisheries resources, are facing increasing pressures from urbanization, industrial activities, and climate change. This project aims to establish an integrated monitoring of five estuaries, combining physicochemical, microbiological, and eDNA analyses with participatory monitoring by local communities. It will assess fishery and microbial biodiversity, as well as ocean-estuary fluxes, and map vulnerable areas. The results will provide reliable data for sustainable coastal management, strengthen local capacities, and contribute to food security, coastal resilience, and the achievement of the Ocean Decade objectives.",
